{
  "_comment": "Feature 14: drag physics. The SDK's own Cubism rig (physics3.json) is driven by head/body PARAMETERS, never by her screen position - so dragging her (Alt/Shift+drag pans the model, plain drag moves the pet) does not move the physics. This adds an inertia overlay on top of the engine: spring-dampers on the rig's soft outputs (hair, fringe, clothes, skirt, ears, chest) driven by the ACCELERATION of her body on screen. sign: -1 = the hair lags behind the motion (physical); flip to +1 if a group swings the wrong way. The spring is deliberately SOFT and slow (stiffness 14, damping 5) so the swing is a lazy, heavy sway instead of a twitch - raise stiffness for a snappier hair, lower it for a slower one. gain_scale multiplies every group's gain at once (0.5 = half strength). max_offset is the clamp in param units. enabled: false removes the whole feature instantly.",
